  "note": "21 subtopics, above the usual 4-15, because the chapter carries 21 numbered headings; every passage is covered exactly once. Two short self-contained blocks got their own named subtopics: 'Polygenic inheritance' (P66) and 'Pleiotropy' (P67). The chapter's own contents list in P03 names only six sections (4.1 Mendel's Laws, 4.2 Inheritance of One Gene, 4.3 Inheritance of Two Genes, 4.4 Sex Determination, 4.5 Mutation, 4.6 Genetic Disorders), while the body headings run 4.4 POLYGENIC INHERITANCE, 4.5 PLEIOTROPY, 4.6 SEX DETERMINATION, 4.7 MUTATION, 4.8 GENETIC DISORDERS - i.e. the contents page and the body disagree by two sections. Other judgement calls: P19-P20 (dominance/recessiveness, symbol convention) and P21 (gamete formation without blending) were placed with the Law of Dominance and Law of Segregation subtopics they state rather than with the monohybrid-cross narrative; the untitled figure P34 sits between the Law of Segregation text and the Incomplete Dominance heading and was assigned to Incomplete Dominance; P42-P43 (starch synthesis in pea seeds, one gene product with more than one effect) were kept with the 'explanation of dominance' discussion they conclude rather than with heading 4.5 Pleiotropy; heading 4.8 (P81) was folded into the pedigree-analysis subtopic. Subtopic 21 exists only to cover the SUMMARY (P101) and EXERCISES (P102) passages, which are not themselves a testable idea."
